Article 2 (Missions) The Joint Chiefs of Staff shall be responsible for:
1. Operational command and supervision of combat-oriented operational units of the Army, Navy, and Air Force;
2. Command and supervision of joint units established to conduct joint operations;
3. Conduct of joint and combined operations;
4. Operation of the Joint Chiefs of Staff Meeting;
5. Military strategy planning and determination of requirements for force development;
6. Collection and use of strategic and military intelligence;
7. Planning and execution of military operations;
8. Determination and planning of resource requirements;
9. Civil-military operations, psychological warfare, and information operations;
9-2. Direction and supervision of cyber operations;
10. Command communications affairs;
11. Conduct of integrated defense operations involving civilians, government, and the military;
12. Affairs relating to martial law;
13. Establishment of smooth consultation systems with the Army, Navy, and Air Force for joint operational support;
14. Guidance and supervision of joint combat development and joint education of the armed services;
15. Other affairs related to subparagraphs 1 through 14. <Amended on December 27, 2012; November 4, 2014; February 16, 2015>
